-- title:
--   Q SDD Right Placed Zero Proj Sub Meas Le One
-- statement:
--   **The zero projective submeasurement is a unit-distance fallback on Bob's register.**
--
--   Let $\psi$ be a normalized quantum state on $H_A\otimes H_B$, and let $A=\{A_a\}$ be any submeasurement on $H_B$ with finite outcome set. Let $0$ denote the projective submeasurement whose every effect is the zero operator. Then the right-placed family of $A$ is at most unit distance from the right-placed zero family:
--
--   $$
--   \operatorname{qSDD}_{\psi}\!\left(I_{H_A}\otimes A,\,I_{H_A}\otimes0\right)\le1.
--   $$
--
--   Normalization of $\psi$ is the only state assumption. This estimate supplies the large-error fallback for `rightPlacedProjectivizationRepair_of_sourceAlmostProjective_two_mul`.
--
--   Formalization credit: Sirui Lu, Ruixuan Deng, Yanqiao Zhu, and Zhengfeng Ji (arXiv:2609.19814). Mathematical source: Zhengfeng Ji, Anand Natarajan, Thomas Vidick, John Wright, and Henry Yuen (arXiv:2009.12982).
--
--   **Formalization Note.** The source declaration is `MIPStarRE.LDT.MakingMeasurementsProjective.qSDD_rightPlaced_zeroProjSubMeas_le_one`; its Lean statement gives the exact quantifier order and all boundary hypotheses.
